# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# DISABLED ON PURPOSE — `.disabled` because ArgoCD's directory recursion only
# reads .yaml/.yml/.json, the same mechanism the mcp-slack Application uses.
#
# NOT because the ciphertext is unfinished. It is sealed against this
# cluster's live controller and `kubeseal --validate` passes.
#
# It is inert because namespace `mcp-slack` DOES NOT EXIST YET, and the app
# that owns this directory does not create namespaces — check
# gitops/argocd/applications/sealed-secrets-manifests.yaml: no
# CreateNamespace=true, prune and selfHeal both on. Measured, not assumed:
# `kubectl apply --dry-run=server` on this file returns
# `namespaces "mcp-slack" not found`, while the identical manifest retargeted
# at an existing namespace applies clean. So enabling it early does not
# produce an unsynced secret — it turns a healthy, self-healing PLATFORM app
# red, which is a wider blast radius than the app it belongs to.
#
# TO ENABLE: drop the `.disabled` suffix AFTER namespace mcp-slack exists.
# The mcp-slack Application creates it (CreateNamespace=true), so enable that
# first; this file is not what gates it.
#
# DO NOT RENAME THE SECRET OR MOVE THE NAMESPACE. Sealed at the default STRICT
# scope, so the ciphertext is bound to name `mcp-slack-tokens` in namespace
# `mcp-slack`. Changing either makes the controller refuse to decrypt, and the
# symptom is a Secret that never appears rather than an error on this object.
#
# Keys are SLACK_BOT_TOKEN and SLACK_TEAM_ID and nothing else, matching the
# two secretKeyRefs in mcp-slack/deploy/chart/templates/deployment.yaml.
# No user token is ever mounted on this path — the bot token only.
#
# Bot U0BNJ3RK9KP, app A0BNFAEKRMH, team T08JV4QGT71 (ABRIAL). The plaintext
# this was sealed from has been deleted.
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
apiVersion: bitnami.com/v1alpha1
kind: SealedSecret
metadata:
  name: mcp-slack-tokens
  namespace: mcp-slack
spec:
  encryptedData:
    SLACK_BOT_TOKEN: 
    SLACK_TEAM_ID: 
  template:
    metadata:
      name: mcp-slack-tokens
      namespace: mcp-slack
